---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-diagram-minimap</code> shows every node of a diagram canvas as a box and the part in view as a
  rectangle, wherever the view has wandered. Click to fly there, or drag to move the view. Put it in the canvas's
  <code>minimap</code> slot, or anywhere with <code>for</code> set to the canvas's id. Size it with
  <code>--diagram-minimap-width</code> and <code>--diagram-minimap-height</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-diagram id="minimap-diagram" start-position="first" style="height: 380px;">
    <wc-diagram-minimap slot="minimap"></wc-diagram-minimap>
  </wc-diagram>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const diagram = document.querySelector('#minimap-diagram');
      const nodes = [];
      const edges = [];
      for (let i = 0; i < 12; i += 1) {
        nodes.push({ id: `n${i}`, position: { x: (i % 4) * 420, y: Math.floor(i / 4) * 260 }, headline: `Step ${i + 1}`, icon: 'radio_button_unchecked' });
        if (i > 0) edges.push({ id: `e${i}`, source: `n${i - 1}`, target: `n${i}` });
      }
      diagram.nodes = nodes;
      diagram.edges = edges;
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  The minimap is a pointer shortcut. Keyboard users pan the canvas with the arrow keys and use
  <wc-kbd keys="shift+1"></wc-kbd> to fit and <wc-kbd keys="home"></wc-kbd> to go back to the start.
</p>
